---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---
<Base title="How a Listing Optimize works, day by day | Nimbuy" description="From intake to a paste-ready listing in three business days: what you send, what we do each day, and what you receive.">
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="label">Process</p>
      <h1>Three business days, start to paste-ready.</h1>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width:56ch">Here is exactly what happens in a Listing Optimize, so you know what to send and what lands in your inbox.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="timeline">
        <div class="tl-item reveal">
          <p class="tl-when">DAY 0 · YOU</p>
          <div>
            <h3>Send the brief and the intake</h3>
            <p>A short brief, then the intake form. The three-day clock starts when the intake comes back, not when you pay.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Listing URL and who buys the product</li>
              <li>Top three alternatives and what you do better than each</li>
              <li>How you price outside Marketplace</li>
              <li>Security facts you can show: certifications, data location, retention, subprocessors</li>
              <li>Anything you are allowed to cite: one-pager, security overview, case study</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item reveal">
          <p class="tl-when">DAY 1 · AUDIT</p>
          <div>
            <h3>Four-reader check</h3>
            <p>Your listing is read as a security reviewer, a procurement analyst, a technical evaluator and an AI search layer would read it. Each of the 12 reviewer questions is marked Yes, Partly or No, with the listing's own sentence quoted as evidence.</p>
            <ul>
              <li>“Answers X of 12” count, with what is missing for each reader</li>
              <li>7-dimension score strip</li>
              <li>The single most expensive gap, named</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item reveal">
          <p class="tl-when">DAY 2 · REWRITE</p>
          <div>
            <h3>Field-by-field rewrite</h3>
            <p>Title, short description, long description, highlights, keywords and pricing-unit wording. Your facts only. Every number carries a source or a date. Adjectives that cannot be checked are cut.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item reveal">
          <p class="tl-when">DAY 3 · DELIVER</p>
          <div>
            <h3>Paste-ready set, plus the co-sell kit</h3>
            <p>You receive the audit, the rewritten listing and, if you have a live AWS deal, a co-sell kit: the email to your AWS rep, an opportunity summary and a five-day follow-up. With no live deal you get a handover note instead, so the listing stays current as the product changes.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="tl-item reveal">
          <p class="tl-when">DAY 3–8 · REVISE</p>
          <div>
            <h3>One revision round</h3>
            <p>Tell us what to change within five business days of delivery. You paste the new copy into your listing yourself; no access to your AWS account is needed.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CtaBand title="Start with the free audit." text="It shows which of the four readers your listing fails first." />
</Base>
